  (text "ISOLATION BARRIER — U201 separates GND (logic) from CAN_GND (bus).\nNo copper on ANY layer may cross under the ADM3053: no pour, no plane, no\nstitching vias. CAN_GND must stay galvanically separate from GND everywhere."
    (at 60 128 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 2 2)))
    (uuid "85c8a765-2c3f-44ed-b985-85c828781b62"))

  (text "dbCAN wiring per d&b TI 312: RJ45 pin 4 = CAN_H, pin 5 = CAN_L,\nSHELL = CAN ground (carried on the cable shield — shielded jacks are mandatory).\nJ201/J202 are wired in PARALLEL so amplifiers daisy-chain, exactly as the R70 does.\nPins 1,2,3,6,7,8 are unused by dbCAN and are flagged no-connect.\nBus is CAN 2.0A, 11-bit IDs, 100 kbit/s fixed."
    (at 150 148 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)))
    (uuid "4a25d5e3-a641-4836-9566-6d8c5a61b20f"))

  (text "Split termination: 2x62R with C207 to CAN_GND = 120R differential plus a\ncommon-mode path. SW201 is 2-pole so BOTH legs break — an SPST would leave an\nasymmetric 62R+C stub on CANL when open. The R70 uses a plain switched 120R;\nthis is deliberately better for EMC. R201 sets ADM3053 slope control: fit 0R for\nhigh speed, or 10k-100k to slow the edges (100 kbit/s has ample margin)."
    (at 150 163 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)))
    (uuid "316a424a-c774-42e7-abe7-ef5ef200a837"))

